Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:13:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11310/11362] Close five holes the adversarial review found in
 the worktree-corpus fix (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6642)

The first version of this fix (8eae2c3986) claimed two things that were
false on the live repository. Both are corrected here, with the record
appended rather than rewritten.

HIGH 1. "An explicit --runs-dir that is missing or empty still fails" was
false for empty. The tracked flat eval results/arc_leaderboard_eval.json
counted as an artifact, so an empty runs directory reported 1 artifact(s)
and passed. artifact_keys now returns the runs-directory count separately
and the fail-closed check keys on it. The flat eval still joins when a run
corpus exists. That wiring had no test before: deleting it left the suite
GREEN. Two tests pin both halves.

HIGH 2. python/carnot/agentic/ is both a consumer tree and the producer
surface, so a consumer there satisfied the producer-source join with its own
EVAL_RUN_FIELDS_READ literal. Measured: the same body failed at scripts/ and
passed at python/carnot/agentic/. The mechanism predates this fix; skip mode
made it the sole gate for a corpus-less checkout. A consumer's own file no
longer vouches for itself (producer_literals_by_file, per-file exclusion).
The one live consumer there, arc_supervisor_refinement.py, still passes.
New scenario SCENARIO-ARC-WMTE-6642-SELF-VOUCH.

Finding 4. git -C does not override GIT_DIR, and git sets GIT_DIR for
worktree hooks, so main_checkout_root answered about whatever repository the
environment named. A non-repository root with GIT_DIR pointing at this
worktree attached this repository's corpus and turned a failure into a pass.
The git subprocess now drops GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_COMMON_DIR and
GIT_INDEX_FILE. GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES stays: it can only shorten discovery.

Finding 5. "Population counts are always printed" was false on two failure
branches. The producer surface is now read before the runs directory is
resolved, so every branch prints a true population line.

Finding 3 is a record correction, not a code change. My 13-probe sweep
pointed --confcutdir only at a checkout root, the one direction that cannot
cut a conftest below it, and then I wrote "closed set". Measured after the
review: --confcutdir deep inside the worktree, cwd in main, PYTHONPATH unset
collects 10 tests with no conftest and carnot from main. The hole is the
tests/ subdirectories with no conftest of their own (archive, fixtures,
quarantine). Appended to the ledger row and ops/status.md.

Proof: 19 mutations (the 13 from 8eae2c3986 plus six for these findings),
19 RED, cmp byte-identical restores, final GREEN, unlocked. 26 tests.

